  {
    "id": "anno-sakurai_lower_p057_right-16",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "附箋"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "附箋（ふせん）＝原本に貼り付けられた紙片。下の括弧（合掌符）が及ぶ範囲を示す。"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Editorial notation printed horizontally (reading right to left) above a brace with downturned ends: 附箋, fusen, an 'attached slip'. The brace runs from inside the 雜稅 現米 column to inside the 正租 現米 column, covering 正租 現米, 正租 永 and 雜稅 現米 but stopping short of the 雜稅 永 column — the arbitrary span one would expect of a paper slip physically pasted onto the original manuscript. The 1928 reprint's collators use the same notation elsewhere in the source, spelled out in full on lower_p018_right (Koromo) as 「（附箋）此分二枚調書取捨よろしく」."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "附箋"
      }
    ],
